 "title": "ZnS QDs and S. cerevisiae Interactions",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the interactions between ZnS QDs and the organism S. cerevisiae. S. cerevisiae is exposed to ZnS QDs and ZnSO4, leading to the induction of ROS and modulation of Mitochondrion. The presence of ZnS QDs causes hypersensitivity in pos5Δ, a mutated strain of S. cerevisiae. Additionally, S. cerevisiae correlates with Skatole, which is associated with the CON-DLY group. The cluster also includes various organisms and chemicals, but the primary focus is on the interactions between ZnS QDs and S. cerevisiae.",
